text.section:
Pursuant to Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of Virginia, and without limiting any other provision of general law, a governing body member may be named by the governing body to one or more of the following positions:

Director of emergency management pursuant to § 44-146.19;


Member of a planning district commission pursuant to § 15.2-4203;


Member of a transportation district commission pursuant to § 33.2-1907;


Member of a behavioral health authority board pursuant to Chapter 6 (§ 37.2-600 et seq.) of Title 37.2;


Member of a hospital or health center commission pursuant to Chapter 52 (§ 15.2-5200 et seq.) of Title 15.2;


Member of a community services board pursuant to Chapter 5 (§ 37.2-500 et seq.) of Title 37.2;


Member of a park authority pursuant to Chapter 57 (§ 15.2-5700 et seq.) of Title 15.2;


Member of a detention or other residential care facilities commission pursuant to Article 13 (§ 16.1-315 et seq.) of Chapter 11 of Title 16.1;


Member of a board of directors, governing board or advisory council of an area agency on aging pursuant to § 51.5-135;


Member of a regional jail or jail farm board, pursuant to § 53.1-106 or of a regional jail authority or jail authority pursuant to Article 3.1 (§ 53.1-95.2 et seq.) of Chapter 3 of Title 53.1;


With respect to members of the governing body of a town under 3,500 population, member of an industrial development authority's board of directors pursuant to Chapter 49 (§ 15.2-4900 et seq.) of Title 15.2;


Member of the board of directors, governing board, or advisory council or committee of an airport commission or authority;


Member of a Board of Directors of a Regional Industrial Facility Authority pursuant to Chapter 64 (§ 15.2-6400 et seq.) of Title 15.2;


Member of a local parks and recreation commission;


Member of the Board of the Richmond Ambulance Authority;


Member of a local convention, visitors, or tourism board, authority, or agency; and


Member of the Board of Directors of the Richmond Metropolitan Transportation Authority pursuant to § 33.2-2901.
